  "tokens": [
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// A chart: head, solos, head out. What a jazz musician hands another jazz" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// musician, and the reason `improvise` exists — the middle of this piece is" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// notated as a frame with nothing inside it, because the notes are the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// player's and musa does not invent notes." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//     musa check examples/changes.musa --seed 3" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//     musa render examples/changes.musa --to musicxml" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The export is lossy on purpose and says so: MusicXML has no improvised" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// region, so it carries the realized silence plus a text direction reading" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// `improvise over Dm7 | G7 | Cmaj7`. A player reading the exported part sees" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// the instruction; a program reading it sees a rest. That is stated in" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// `docs/kernel/07-backend-contract.md` rather than discovered." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The last chord is `1 to 4/1`: held as long as the band likes. Its written" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// value is the whole note the engraver draws; what it sounds is the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// performance's answer. Roadmap §2's row — notated duration ≠ performed" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// duration — with both values kept." },
